! `h10-chain-lsda.in` in the **noncollinear** regime: the same ten-site chain
! and the same antiferromagnetic order, but written as `nspin = 4` with the
! moments lying in the xy plane (`angle1 = 90`) and antiparallel to each other
! (`angle2 = 0` and `180`).
!
! Two things are being compared at once. Against QE, it is a `nspin_mag = 4`
! run at ten sites -- the spinor Hamiltonian, the axial-vector symmetrisation
! of the magnetization and the magnetic symmetry group. Against its own
! collinear neighbour, it is the statement that a rotation of every moment by
! the same angle costs nothing: the total energy of the two files must agree to
! the convergence threshold, and QE gives that identity as well.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 12.0, celldm(3) = 4.16666666666667,
    nat = 10, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.10,
    noncolin = .true.,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.6, angle1(1) = 90.0, angle2(1) =   0.0,
    starting_magnetization(2) = 0.6, angle1(2) = 90.0, angle2(2) = 180.0,
    nbnd = 28
 /
 &electrons
    mixing_beta = 0.3
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 H1  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
 H2  1.008  H.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.0
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.1
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.2
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.3
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.4
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.5
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.6
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.7
 H1 0.0 0.0 0.8
 H2 0.0 0.0 0.9
K_POINTS {automatic}
 1 1 2 0 0 0
